---
title: Cheesy Marmite Straws
yield: 20%straw
course: snack
prep time: 20m
cook time: 20m
locale: en
difficulty: medium
---

Preheat oven to 180°C.

Sprinkle a clean work surface with @plain flour{}(for dusting). Lay out the @ready-rolled puff pastry{1%pack}(300 g) sheet, with the longer edge towards you. Lightly spread the pastry sheet with @Marmite{2%tbsp}. Cover the whole pastry sheet with the @cheddar cheese{250%g}(grated). Fold in half from the top down. Coat the rolling pin with some flour (not the pastry), and gently roll out the piece to lengthen it. Don’t roll too thin or the pastry will not puff up.

Line a large #baking tray{} with greaseproof paper. Carefully transfer the pastry to the chopping board and use a sharp knife to cut the pastry into batons about 1.5cm wide. Lay the straws next to each other on the tray. Beat the @egg{1} in a cup and, with a pastry brush, coat each baton with egg. Sprinkle with @parmesan{4%tbsp}(grated), @mild chilli flakes{1%tsp} and @black pepper{}(freshly ground).

Bake for ~{20%minutes} until golden and crisp.